<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zittau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zittau is a town in the south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, near the borders with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>. A wealthy cloth-trading town under the Bohemian crown, it was a founding member of the Six Towns League of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-lusatia">Upper Lusatia</a> in 1346. It is known for its large painted Lenten veils, the oldest from 1472.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zittau.jpg" alt="Zittau" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vit · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C5%BDitava_radnice_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
